\title{Fractional Memory Experiment Design: Active and Safe Discrimination between Fractional, Delayed, and Latent Memory via Optimal Excitation}
\author{Anonymous}
\date{\today}

\begin{document}

\maketitle
\begin{abstract}
This paper presents a definitive experimental design for discriminating between fractional (Caputo), delayed (DDE), and latent (finite-dimensional) memory effects in a predator-prey system with strong Allee effect. The design leverages optimal excitation to exploit structural frequency separation and the finite-horizon impossibility obstacle, around a certified equilibrium of the model \[[CITE-NEEDED: sasmal2018]].
\end{abstract}

